Station H-02 in survey area H consists of a four-layer sequence. The resistivity profile starts at 364.5 ohm-m (0.81m depth), decreases to 257.8 ohm-m (3.34m base), increases to 745.5 ohm-m (15.99m base), and reaches 1146.1 ohm-m in the fourth layer.

Based on these values, the curve-type notation is HA. The first triplet (364.5, 257.8, 745.5) follows an H pattern ($r_1 > r_2 < r_3$), and the second triplet (257.8, 745.5, 1146.1) follows an A pattern ($r_2 < r_3 < r_4$). The survey classification on file as "H-type" is inconsistent with the interpreted resistivity values, as the sequence correctly requires the HA designation.

